,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47132280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe","html_url":"https://github.com/jaydensipe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T08:55:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T08:55:52Z","body":"Seems good.\r\n\r\nAlthough, in this example, is there a way I could exclude the `fps_example.VoxelGI_data.res` from showing? My idea with adding the glob based search was more so for filtering. Could we incorporate the \"fp*.gd\" search in addition to the subsequence search?\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2380\" height=\"410\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/30f8f725-997e-45c8-b410-3d5835afc1b2\" />\r\n&nbsp\r\n\r\nVS (main).\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2051\" height=\"460\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9d8a889-ce0e-4c2e-b909-b7e8e9669a93\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5407918412/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5410976941","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793#issuecomment-5410976941","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793","id":5410976941,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQoT0rQ","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T13:19:51Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T13:19:51Z","body":"@jaydensipe do you want it to be where if an \"*\" is included, then only file names are searched and the stricter search is used (basically your implementation)? Otherwise, (default) would search the whole file path with subsequence (my implementation).\r\n\r\nI still found it a bit odd that I couldn't search the folder name with your implementation, what do you think about having `**` allow searching subfolders? So `test**.gd` would find .gd files in the folder `test`, and `a/b/c/test456.gd` and the path `test123/another/folder/file.gd`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5410976941/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5413562147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793#issuecomment-5413562147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793","id":5413562147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQqxnIw","user":{"login":"NicholasBolen","id":98554429,"node_id":"U_kgDOBd_SPQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98554429?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen","html_url":"https://github.com/NicholasBolen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NicholasBolen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T16:35:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T16:36:40Z","body":"VSCode file search seems to fuzzy search the file path, prioritizing the file name (this matches Godot's \"Select resource\" search). AFAICT glob based search is not used, only appearing when filtering files in find/replace.\r\n\r\nIf matches were sorted, glob support might be less necessary.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"908\" height=\"308\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/53645498-03e6-4ba3-a790-a085523a994e\" />\r\n\r\nVSCode's find/replace search supports path segment globs with * (also matches path!), and uses ** to consume 0 or more path segments.\r\n\r\nThe sample `test**.gd` doesn't quite work like that (in VSCode), ** is just for consuming nested folders. Rules are [here](https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/editor/glob-patterns), but actually testing them they feel a bit confusing.\r\n\r\nWherever this filtering ends up, I'd suggest it be based on existing behaviour.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5413562147/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5418009092","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793#issuecomment-5418009092","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793","id":5418009092,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQvBCBA","user":{"login":"jaydensipe","id":47132280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTMyMjgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47132280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe","html_url":"https://github.com/jaydensipe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T22:56:47Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T22:57:34Z","body":"I agree with whatever it ends up being, should be based on existing behavior as well. \r\n\r\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/extensions/file-globbing. I was reading and this seems to be a decent reference.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1667\" height=\"1302\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d839e05-c21a-47e0-8dcb-6c011756884d\" />\r\n\r\nSo with this I'd assume:\r\n\r\nfp*.gd - Shows all .gd files beginning with fp in the project.\r\ntest/**/*.gd - Shows all .gd files in all subdirectories under the root **test** directory.\r\n**/materials/\\* - Show all files under a nested **materials** directory.\r\ntest/\\* - Could then maybe show all files under a root **test** directory?\r\n\r\n--\r\n\r\n> @jaydensipe do you want it to be where if an \"*\" is included, then only file names are searched and the stricter search is used (basically your implementation)? Otherwise, (default) would search the whole file path with subsequence (my implementation).\r\n\r\nI could see this working, allowing the \"*\" for filtering as needed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5418009092/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5420454283","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793#issuecomment-5420454283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793","id":5420454283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQxWRiw","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648","html_url":"https://github.com/Goldenlion5648","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Goldenlion5648/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T04:09:43Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T04:11:13Z","body":"The PR has been redone to incorporate glob search according to the microsoft page specification, see the new video/ description.\r\n\r\nMaybe the glob search code could be extracted to the string class so it can be used elsewhere?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5420454283/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433007688","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793#issuecomment-5433007688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793","id":5433007688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ9UeSA","user":{"login":"jaydensipe","id":47132280,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MTMyMjgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47132280?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe","html_url":"https://github.com/jaydensipe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jaydensipe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T01:08:07Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T01:08:07Z","body":"Works great now! Although, I think there is an issue when using the **split FileSystem**, causing the files not to show.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e40f79fe-6676-4166-9fba-c88a69a24405\r\n\r\n--\r\n\r\nAs for the String question, I think it can be a good idea, but I'd definitely get an answer from someone with a bit more authority before you go ahead with it.\r\n\r\nFor the \"Filter Files\" placeholder as well, perhaps we should show an example filter, something like Zed does?\r\n\r\n<img width=\"772\" height=\"100\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7afa3046-c535-4c00-adc0-e0d18cc4ecfa\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433007688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433179947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793#issuecomment-5433179947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793","id":5433179947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ9e_Kw","user":{"login":"Goldenlion5648","id":32916571,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTE2NTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32916571?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"h